  "body": "Documentation required:  The 'id' property of `<form>` gets hijacked when the form contains `<input name='id'>`.\r\n\r\nThis contradicts the agreed upon meaning of \".id\".   \r\n\r\nDocumentation should call-out this fact as a  special case, (or deprecate the notation style \"form.xxx\").\r\n\r\nHere is a minimal test case illustrating the issue.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n  <meta name=\"author\" content=\"Alexander Danel\">\r\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An <input name=id> hijacks '.id' property of <form>\">\r\n  <title>\"Input w name=id hijacks form '.id' property\"</title>\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"form_holder\">\r\n  <form id=\"foo123\">\r\n    <input name=\"id\" value=\"Hello World\">\r\n  </form>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\n var formHolderEl = document.getElementById(\"form_holder\");\r\n var formEl = formHolderEl.firstElementChild;\r\n\r\n console.log(\"What is the value of the '.id' property? \", formEl.id);\r\n // =>  <input name=\"id\" value=\"Hello World\">\r\n\r\n console.log(\"Which mimics the 'elements' array:\", formEl.elements[\"id\"]);\r\n // =>  <input name=\"id\" value=\"Hello World\">\r\n\r\n console.log(\"The 'attributes' retain correct value:\", formEl.getAttribute(\"id\"));\r\n // foo123\r\n\r\n console.log(\"Issue does not impede getting by id: \", document.getElementById(\"foo123\"));\r\n // => <form id=\"foo123\">...</form>\r\n\r\n</script>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
